    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by high-floor matchups and stolen base upside. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.13) stands as our premier start; his elite sprint speed makes him indispensable in our SB-starved Roto environment, and the dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed Luis Castillo elevates his profile to near-elite status. Joining him as a top-tier option is **Trea Turner** (74.58), whose leadoff-adjacent presence against the soft-tossing Junk provides an optimal environment for R and SB accumulation. **Kyle Schwarber** (73.46) similarly benefits from the matchup against Junk, maintaining his strong projection despite the slight negative adjustment for platoon dynamics, as his power-speed contribution in the top of the order remains a staple of our daily offensive floor.\n\nEfficiency metrics suggest **Caleb Durbin** (67.03) and **Junior Caminero** (70.15) are essential components of today\u2019s strategy. **Caleb Durbin** benefits from an inviting 5.58 xERA matchup, though we must monitor the 30% rain risk hovering over that contest. While **Colt Keith** (60.53) and **Carson Benge** (58.65) sit in the middle tier, both are locked in due to reliable order positioning and favorable SP skill matchups. The decision to bench secondary depth options\u2014such as **Nelson Velazquez**, **Casey Schmitt**, or **Josh Smith**\u2014was largely dictated by the optimizer\u2019s preference for the higher ceiling offered by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner** in their specific matchups. **Lars Nootbaar** (42.84) represents our most marginal start today; his low score is a consequence of an 8-hole assignment and a challenging platoon disadvantage, leaving him on the verge of being benched for bench depth like **Hector Rodriguez** or **Jacob Gonzalez** should late-breaking injury news emerge. \n\nWe remain cognizant of the limitations elsewhere in the roster. **Dillon Dingler** (45.71) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (52.20) are strictly \"marginal\" plays, capped by sub-optimal platoon splits and park factors. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Gary Sanchez** all unavailable due to scheduled off-days, our reliance on utility depth\u2014including **Luis Pena** and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014is non-existent today. The primary focus remains on maintaining our SB advantage while leveraging the high-volume opportunities for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin**. Caution is advised regarding the weather-impacted games for **Caleb Durbin** and **Lars Nootbaar**; we will adjust the outfield alignment if the precipitation forecast worsens.",
